    {
      "id": "6hh8j5y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Divergent Boundaries"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tectonic plate interactions are categorized into three primary structural boundary types.",
        "Divergent boundaries occur where tectonic plates move away from each other.",
        "Convergent boundaries occur where tectonic plates collide or move toward each other.",
        "Transform boundaries occur where tectonic plates slide horizontally past one another."
      ],
      "id": "p7pznzx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zhxk5bh",
      "content": "• Magma rises to fill the gap created by separating plates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jzz5a5b",
      "content": "• Produces mid-ocean ridges such as the Mid-Atlantic Ridge."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Types of Plate Boundaries",
      "id": "p79x3ka"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9edaubi",
      "content": "• On continents, divergence forms rift valleys like the East African Rift."
    },
    {
      "id": "k3nxgaw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Convergent Boundaries"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Boundary Type",
        "Plate Movement"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Divergent Boundaries",
          "Plates move away from each other"
        ],
        [
          "Convergent Boundaries",
          "Plates move toward each other"
        ],
        [
          "Transform Boundaries",
          "Plates slide past each other horizontally"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "0ia8xhm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aywpcmc",
      "content": "• Oceanic–continental convergence forms volcanic mountain chains."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kdohaxc",
      "content": "• Oceanic–oceanic convergence forms island arcs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qhgms2f",
      "content": "• Continental–continental collision forms large fold mountains such as the Himalayas."
    },
    {
      "id": "dbsotlm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Transform Boundaries"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
